1. Bootloader loads kernel and switches to protected mode.
2. Kernel initializes ATA and reads sector 19 (root directory).
3. Kernel searches for a file named `TEST.TXT`.
4. Kernel reads the file’s data cluster and prints it (via VGA or serial).

